"translation":null,"userId":"uid_1778159494233_wkl8keakk","characterId":"996d4ccc-2914-4aa4-9ba8-c100ab38b933","_id":9495},{"id":1781667582369,"text":"This is an artwork refinement task, not a redesign task.\n\nPreserve all existing lineart and shapes.\n\nDo not modify the character's face, clothing design, pose, hand position, card arrangement, mechanical arm structure, background architecture or camera angle.This is an artwork refinement task, not a redesign task.\n\nPreserve all existing lineart, composition, character design, pose, card arrangement, mechanical arms, invitation card, table layout and background architecture.\n\nDo not change the face, clothing, silhouette, camera angle or overall composition.\n\nEstablish a clear primary light source from the upper-left candlelight area.\n\nUse warm golden candlelight as the main light source and cool blue cyberpunk city light as secondary ambient lighting.\n\nImprove the artwork as if it is in the final polishing stage of a professional visual novel illustration.\n\nAdd stronger and cleaner cel-shaded shadows under the hat brim, collar, sleeves and mechanical arms.\n\nFocus on material rendering:\n\n- leather top hat with subtle specular highlights\n- metallic robotic arms with clean hard reflections\n- transparent wine glass with realistic glass highlights\n- glossy playing cards with slight reflected light\n- gold invitation card with elegant metallic reflections\n\nAdd subtle table reflections from candlelight and cards.\n\nImprove depth and readability while keeping the image mostly cel-shaded.\n\nAvoid messy shadows.\n\nAvoid excessive painterly rendering.\n\nAvoid over-detailing.\n\nAvoid redesigning any element.\n\nFocus on unified lighting, material definition and visual polish.\n\nThe final result should feel like a finished official game key visual.","sender":"me","time":"11:40","timestamp":1781667614926,"replyTo":null,"userId":"uid_1778159494233_wkl8keakk","characterId":"996d4ccc-2914-4aa4-9ba8-c100ab